#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:6
msgid "RHEL (binary)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:10
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:12
msgid ""
"This page explains how to install ROS 2 on RHEL from a pre-built binary "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:16
msgid ""
"The pre-built binary does not include all ROS 2 packages. All packages in "
"the `ROS base variant <https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-2001/#ros-base>`_ "
"are included, and only a subset of packages in the `ROS desktop variant "
"<https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-2001/#desktop-variants>`_ are included. "
"The exact list of packages are described by the repositories listed in `this "
"ros2.repos file <https://github.com/ros2/ros2/blob/rolling/ros2.repos>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:20
msgid "There are also :doc:`RPM packages <../RHEL-Install-RPMs>` available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:23
msgid "System requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:25
msgid ""
"We currently support RHEL 10 64-bit. The Rolling Ridley distribution will "
"change target platforms from time to time as new platforms are selected for "
"development. Most people will want to use a stable ROS distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:30
msgid "System setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:33
msgid "Set locale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_RHEL-Set-Locale.rst:5
msgid ""
"Make sure you have a locale which supports ``UTF-8``. If you are in a "
"minimal environment (such as a docker container), the locale may be "
"something minimal like ``C``. We test with the following settings. However, "
"it should be fine if you're using a different UTF-8 supported locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_RHEL-Set-Locale.rst:10
msgid ""
"$ locale  # check for UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ sudo dnf install langpacks-en glibc-langpack-en\n"
"$ export LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ locale  # verify settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:38
msgid "Enable required repositories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:40
msgid ""
"The rosdep database contains packages from the EPEL and PowerTools "
"repositories, which are not enabled by default. They can be enabled by "
"running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:43
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf install 'dnf-command(config-manager)' epel-release -y\n"
"$ sudo dnf config-manager --set-enabled crb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:48
msgid ""
"This step may be slightly different depending on the distribution you are "
"using. `Check the EPEL documentation <https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/"
"epel/#_quickstart>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:52
msgid "Install prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:54
msgid ""
"There are a few packages that must be installed in order to get and unpack "
"the binary release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:56
msgid "$ sudo dnf install tar bzip2 wget -y"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:61
msgid "Install development tools (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:63
msgid ""
"If you are going to build ROS packages or otherwise do development, you can "
"also install the development tools:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:65
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf install -y \\\n"
"  cmake \\\n"
"  gcc-c++ \\\n"
"  git \\\n"
"  make \\\n"
"  patch \\\n"
"  python3-colcon-common-extensions \\\n"
"  python3-mypy \\\n"
"  python3-pip \\\n"
"  python3-pytest \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-repeat \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-rerunfailures \\\n"
"  python3-rosdep \\\n"
"  python3-setuptools \\\n"
"  python3-vcstool \\\n"
"  wget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:85
msgid "Install ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:87
msgid ""
"Binary releases of Rolling Ridley are not provided. Instead you may download "
"nightly :ref:`prerelease binaries <Prerelease_binaries>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:90
msgid ""
"Download the latest package for RHEL; let's assume that it ends up at ``~/"
"Downloads/ros2-package-linux-x86_64.tar.bz2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:92
msgid ""
"Note: there may be more than one binary download option which might cause "
"the file name to differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:94
msgid "Unpack it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:96
msgid ""
"$ mkdir -p ~/ros2_rolling\n"
"$ cd ~/ros2_rolling\n"
"$ tar xf ~/Downloads/ros2-package-linux-x86_64.tar.bz2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:103
msgid "Install dependencies using rosdep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Dnf-Update-Admonition.rst:5
msgid ""
"ROS 2 packages are built on frequently updated RHEL systems. It is always "
"recommended that you ensure your system is up to date before installing new "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Dnf-Update-Admonition.rst:8
msgid "$ sudo dnf update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:107
msgid ""
"$ sudo rosdep init\n"
"$ rosdep update\n"
"$ rosdep install --from-paths ~/ros2_rolling/ros2-linux/share --ignore-src -"
"y --skip-keys \"cyclonedds fastcdr fastdds iceoryx_binding_c rti-connext-"
"dds-7.7.0 urdfdom_headers\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:114
msgid "Install additional RMW implementations (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:116
msgid ""
"The default middleware that ROS 2 uses is ``Fast DDS``, but the middleware "
"(RMW) can be replaced at runtime. See the :doc:`guide <../RMW-"
"Implementations/Working-with-multiple-RMW-implementations>` on how to work "
"with multiple RMWs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:120
msgid "Setup environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:122
msgid "Set up your environment by sourcing the following file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:124
msgid "$ . ~/ros2_rolling/ros2-linux/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:130
msgid ""
"Replace ``.bash`` with your shell if you're not using bash. Possible values "
"are: ``setup.bash``, ``setup.sh``, ``setup.zsh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:134
msgid "Try some examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:136
msgid "In one terminal, source the setup file and then run a C++ ``talker``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:138
msgid ""
"$ . ~/ros2_rolling/ros2-linux/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:143
msgid ""
"In another terminal source the setup file and then run a Python ``listener``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:145
msgid ""
"$ . ~/ros2_rolling/ros2-linux/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:150
msgid ""
"You should see the ``talker`` saying that it's ``Publishing`` messages and "
"the ``listener`` saying ``I heard`` those messages. This verifies both the C+"
"+ and Python APIs are working properly. Hooray!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:155
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:157
msgid ""
"Continue with the tutorials to configure your environment, create your own "
"workspace and packages, and learn ROS 2 core concepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:160
msgid "Troubleshoot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:162
msgid ""
"Troubleshooting techniques can be found :doc:`here <../Installation-"
"Troubleshooting>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:165
msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:167
msgid ""
"If you installed your workspace with colcon as instructed above, "
"\"uninstalling\" could be just a matter of opening a new terminal and not "
"sourcing the workspace's ``setup`` file. This way, your environment will "
"behave as though there is no Rolling install on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:170
msgid ""
"If you're also trying to free up space, you can delete the entire workspace "
"directory with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Install-Binary.rst:172
msgid "$ rm -rf ~/ros2_rolling"
msgstr ""
